1. Basic BFS Traversal

Idea:
Use Queue
Use visited[]
Start from a source node
Visit all neighbours
Then visit their neighbours

void bfs(int start, ArrayList<Integer>[] graph, int n) {

    boolean[] visited = new boolean[n + 1];

    Queue<Integer> q = new LinkedList<>();

    q.add(start);
    visited[start] = true;

    while(!q.isEmpty()) {

        int node = q.poll();

        System.out.println(node);

        for(int neighbour : graph[node]) {

            if(!visited[neighbour]) {

                visited[neighbour] = true;
                q.add(neighbour);
            }
        }
    }
}

Core pattern:
Queue
  ↓
take node
  ↓
visit neighbours
  ↓
unvisited → mark + add to queue

Time: O(N + M)
Space: O(N + M) for graph + BFS structures.
